{"id": "2026-10-09-news-navi-pillay-wins-nobel-peace-prize", "date": "2026-10-09", "stream": "news", "headline": "Navi Pillay wins Nobel Peace Prize", "summary": "The Norwegian Nobel Committee awarded the 2026 Nobel Peace Prize to South African jurist Navi Pillay for promoting peace and international law.", "url": "https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/peace/2026/press-release/", "source_domain": "nobelprize.org", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["official PR"], "topics": ["world", "geopolitics"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "The Norwegian Nobel Committee awarded the 2026 Nobel Peace Prize on Friday 9 October to Navanethem \"Navi\" Pillay, the South African jurist, \"for her efforts to promote peace and international law.\". Pillay, 85, was born into a family of Indian Tamil origin under apartheid in Durban and defended Nelson Mandela and other anti-apartheid activists before sitting as a judge on South Africa's High Court, the International Criminal Tribunal for Rwanda and the International Criminal Court. She was later UN High Commissioner for Human Rights, until recently chaired the UN commission of inquiry on the Occupied Palestinian Territory, and now sits on the International Court of Justice in the case accusing Myanmar of genocide. The committee's statement credits her with helping ensure that war crimes, crimes against humanity and genocide are prosecuted, and says international law and its institutions are \"under tremendous pressure.\" The committee received 287 nominations this year, Al Jazeera reports.", "why": "the committee chose a judge rather than a peace deal or a negotiator, and its citation reads as a direct defence of international courts at a time when governments are openly attacking them.", "thread_id": "2026-10-09-news-navi-pillay-wins-nobel-peace-prize", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-09", "event_date": "2026-10-09", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Navi Pillay", "Nobel Peace Prize", "International Court of Justice", "South Africa"]}
{"id": "2026-10-09-news-trump-rules-out-iran-strikes-until-midterms", "date": "2026-10-09", "stream": "news", "headline": "Trump rules out Iran strikes until midterms", "summary": "Trump said the US will not attack Iran before the 3 November midterms while reporting says US forces in the region are growing.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/us-will-not-resume-strikes-on-iran-before-midterms-trump/a-79603731", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "US President Donald Trump posted on Thursday 8 October that the US \"will not be attacking Iran at any time prior to the midterm elections\" on Tuesday 3 November, and said his team was \"having productive discussions\" with Tehran. He posted this after US outlets reported that he was weighing new strikes, and The Atlantic reported that the aim was to keep a deeply unpopular war out of the news until the vote. Treat the pledge with caution. It has a built-in expiry date. The US–Iran ceasefire agreed in April did not hold. Trump told the UN General Assembly he could still escalate, and he rejected an Iranian proposal at the end of September to reopen the Strait of Hormuz to shipping. DW, citing the Wall Street Journal, reports that a third US aircraft-carrier strike group is due in the region by the end of November. Iran's foreign minister said Tehran would answer a US response to its Hormuz plan within days.", "why": "the post rules out strikes only until polling day, and US military forces in the region are still growing.", "thread_id": "2026-10-09-news-trump-rules-out-iran-strikes-until-midterms", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-09", "event_date": "2026-10-08", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Donald Trump", "Iran", "United States", "Strait of Hormuz"]}
{"id": "2026-10-09-news-ukraine-us-and-europeans-meet-in-miami", "date": "2026-10-09", "stream": "news", "headline": "Ukraine, US and Europeans meet in Miami", "summary": "Ukrainian negotiators meet Witkoff and Kushner in Miami on 9-10 October with European advisers invited, after deadly Russian strikes.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-europe-us-to-meet-in-miami-for-talks-on-ending-war/a-79606735", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Ukrainian negotiators were due to meet US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner in Miami on Friday 9 October and Saturday 10 October for talks on ending Russia's war, Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said. US officials told AFP that the national security advisers of France, Germany and the UK, as well as EU and NATO representatives, had been invited. Zelensky said more than 70 people had been killed in Russian strikes in the previous two days. The delegation includes his chief of staff Kyrylo Budanov and Rustem Umerov. A US source told AFP the talks would cover \"new ideas\" developed in recent contacts with both sides. Zelensky rejected US Secretary of State Marco Rubio's description of the war as a stalemate, which the Kremlin endorsed. He accused Washington of \"unwillingness\" to pressure Moscow and urged it to widen Ukraine's access to Starlink (Elon Musk's satellite-internet service) so Ukraine can target Russian missile launchers.", "why": "these are the first talks with Europeans at the table since Washington started calling the war a stalemate, and they come as Russia steps up strikes ahead of winter.", "thread_id": "2026-10-09-news-ukraine-us-and-europeans-meet-in-miami", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-09", "event_date": "2026-10-09", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Ukraine", "Russia", "Volodymyr Zelensky", "Steve Witkoff", "Jared Kushner"]}
{"id": "2026-10-09-news-maduro-charged-with-torturing-us-citizens", "date": "2026-10-09", "stream": "news", "headline": "Maduro charged with torturing US citizens", "summary": "The US Justice Department unsealed a superseding indictment charging Nicolas Maduro and Cilia Flores with conspiracy to commit torture.", "url": "https://www.justice.gov/opa/pr/nicolas-maduro-moros-and-cilia-adela-flores-de-maduro-charged-torture", "source_domain": "justice.gov", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["official PR"], "topics": ["geopolitics", "world"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The US Justice Department unsealed a superseding indictment on Thursday 8 October that charges former Venezuelan President Nicolás Maduro and his wife, Cilia Flores, with conspiracy to commit torture, including of US citizens, on top of the existing narcoterrorism, cocaine and weapons counts. A superseding indictment replaces an earlier one, usually to add charges. The new filing says the couple \"sat atop\" a system of repression built on arbitrary detention and torture. It describes one US citizen who was held in Venezuela and subjected to simulated drowning, beatings and electric shocks. It also alleges that relatives of a judicial official were tortured until he barred opposition figures from running for office. US special forces seized Maduro and Flores in Caracas in early January, an operation that drew widespread international condemnation. Both have pleaded not guilty to the earlier charges, and Judge Alvin Hellerstein denied Flores pretrial release on the same day.", "why": "the torture count turns a drug case into a human-rights prosecution. It also makes the legality of how the defendants were brought to New York more prominent.", "thread_id": "2026-10-09-news-maduro-charged-with-torturing-us-citizens", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-09", "event_date": "2026-10-08", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Nicolas Maduro", "Cilia Flores", "Venezuela", "US Department of Justice"]}
{"id": "2026-10-09-news-ethiopian-drones-hit-eritrean-troops-in-tigray", "date": "2026-10-09", "stream": "news", "headline": "Ethiopian drones hit Eritrean troops in Tigray", "summary": "Ethiopian government drones struck Eritrean troops who crossed into Tigray, according to ACLED.", "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/08/ethiopia-drone-attack-against-eritrean-troops-in-tigray", "source_domain": "theguardian.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Ethiopian government drones struck Eritrean troops who had crossed into Ethiopia's Tigray region on Wednesday 7 October and Thursday 8 October, according to ACLED (Armed Conflict Location & Event Data, a conflict-monitoring group). Witnesses and a militia commander said the Eritrean vehicles reached Adigrat, about 40 km south of the border. Eritrea's information minister would neither confirm nor deny that its troops were in Ethiopia. The Tigray People's Liberation Front (TPLF) launched an offensive against the federal government on 23 September. A government-allied militia took Tigray's capital, Mekelle, on 4 October after the TPLF withdrew. Ethiopian Prime Minister Abiy Ahmed's talk of a right to Red Sea access has made Eritrea fear an invasion.", "why": "this is the first reported direct clash between the two states' forces since their 2018 rapprochement. Analysts fear it could turn Ethiopia's internal fighting into a regional war.", "thread_id": "2026-10-09-news-ethiopian-drones-hit-eritrean-troops-in-tigray", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-09", "event_date": "2026-10-07", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Ethiopia", "Eritrea", "Tigray", "TPLF"]}
{"id": "2026-10-09-news-brazil-judge-orders-eduardo-bolsonaro-s-arrest", "date": "2026-10-09", "stream": "news", "headline": "Brazil judge orders Eduardo Bolsonaro's arrest", "summary": "Justice de Moraes ordered Eduardo Bolsonaro arrested to serve a four-year sentence, weeks before the 25 October runoff.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/9/brazilian-supreme-court-judge-issues-arrest-warrant-for-eduardo-bolsonaro", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["politics", "world"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Brazilian Supreme Court Justice Alexandre de Moraes ordered the arrest of Eduardo Bolsonaro on Thursday 8 October and said he must start serving immediately the four-year sentence he received in June. Eduardo is the brother of presidential candidate Flávio Bolsonaro and lives in Texas. He was convicted of lobbying Washington to sanction Brazilian officials and raise tariffs on Brazilian goods during his father Jair Bolsonaro's coup trial. De Moraes also cancelled his passport. The order comes before the Sunday 25 October runoff between President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva and Flávio Bolsonaro, whom Al Jazeera describes as the favourite to win. The Bolsonaros regard de Moraes as a political enemy.", "why": "a ruling against a close relative of the frontrunner, weeks before the vote, will feed both camps' accusations of \"lawfare\".", "thread_id": "2026-10-09-news-brazil-judge-orders-eduardo-bolsonaro-s-arrest", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-09", "event_date": "2026-10-08", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Eduardo Bolsonaro", "Flavio Bolsonaro", "Alexandre de Moraes", "Brazil"]}
{"id": "2026-10-09-news-low-rhine-forces-first-ever-feed-reserve-release", "date": "2026-10-09", "stream": "news", "headline": "Low Rhine forces first-ever feed-reserve release", "summary": "Parmelin ordered the release of compulsory protein-feed reserves as low Rhine and Danube water chokes imports.", "url": "https://www.bwl.admin.ch/de/newnsb/VsI1z9jOLUgq", "source_domain": "bwl.admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["official PR", "new source"], "topics": ["switzerland", "economy"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Economy Minister Guy Parmelin on Thursday 8 October ordered the release of Switzerland's compulsory reserves of protein feed for livestock, because low water on the Rhine and Danube is choking imports. The ordinance takes effect on Thursday 15 October. Under a temporary overdraft allowed since 1 September, companies have already drawn 9.5% of the stocks. The Federal Office for National Economic Supply says this is the first time compulsory food or feed reserves have ever actually been used. In 2018, also a low-water year, withdrawals were authorised but never needed. The reserves are meant to cover two months with no imports at all. Because some feed still arrives, the office expects them to last much longer, and it says supply on world markets is ample: the bottleneck is transport. Rail and road freight are already in high demand.", "why": "the Rhine is Switzerland's main bulk-import route, and running it this low tests the country's emergency-stockpile system for the first time.", "thread_id": "2026-10-09-news-low-rhine-forces-first-ever-feed-reserve-release", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-09", "event_date": "2026-10-08", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Federal Office for National Economic Supply", "Guy Parmelin", "Rhine"]}
{"id": "2026-10-09-news-crans-montana-fire-round-table-named", "date": "2026-10-09", "stream": "news", "headline": "Crans-Montana fire round table named", "summary": "The federal government named the round table to negotiate an out-of-court settlement for victims of the Crans-Montana bar fire.", "url": "https://www.admin.ch/fr/newnsb/sWl2llfFOn3r", "source_domain": "admin.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["official PR"], "topics": ["switzerland"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "The federal government published on Thursday 8 October who will sit on the round table that is to negotiate an out-of-court settlement for victims of the 1 January 2026 fire at the Le Constellation bar in Crans-Montana (VS). Its chair, Laurent Kurth, chose lawyers and associations who each speak for several victims' families. Also at the table are the commune of Crans-Montana, the canton of Valais, the Federal Office of Justice, and insurers including AXA, Helvetia and Suva. A separate group of federal offices, insurance associations, the Beloved foundation and a university professor will advise. All victims and relatives will be consulted on draft proposals at several stages. The first session is expected \"this autumn,\" and the government says talks will stay confidential.", "why": "this is the first concrete step towards compensating victims without years of litigation.", "thread_id": "2026-10-09-news-crans-montana-fire-round-table-named", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-09", "event_date": "2026-10-08", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Crans-Montana", "Le Constellation", "Laurent Kurth", "Valais"]}
{"id": "2026-10-09-news-cable-fire-cuts-lausanne-yverdon-rail-line", "date": "2026-10-09", "stream": "news", "headline": "Cable fire cuts Lausanne-Yverdon rail line", "summary": "A cable-duct fire near Eclepens cut SBB traffic between Cossonay-Penthalaz and Chavornay with no forecast for reopening.", "url": "https://www.letemps.ch/articles/un-incendie-interrompt-le-trafic-ferroviaire-entre-lausanne-et-yverdon-les-bains", "source_domain": "letemps.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["switzerland"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "A fire in a cable duct near Eclépens (VD) knocked out a signal box at about 03:15 on Friday 9 October and cut rail traffic between Cossonay-Penthalaz and Chavornay on the Lausanne–Yverdon line. The IC5, IC51, R1 and R2 services are affected, and replacement buses are running. SBB (CFF) advises travellers between the Lake Geneva region and German-speaking Switzerland, and between Neuchâtel and Biel, to go via Bern, Fribourg or Payerne. SBB first said the disruption would last until at least noon but by mid-morning said no forecast was possible. Police are investigating the cause, and repairs can only start once that is done.", "why": "the Jura-foot line is the main route north out of Lausanne, so the closure affects commuters across western Switzerland.", "thread_id": "2026-10-09-news-cable-fire-cuts-lausanne-yverdon-rail-line", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-09", "event_date": "2026-10-09", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["SBB", "Eclepens", "Vaud"]}
{"id": "2026-10-09-news-verkehr-45-draws-road-versus-rail-fight", "date": "2026-10-09", "stream": "news", "headline": "Verkehr '45 draws road-versus-rail fight", "summary": "Consultation responses to the Verkehr 45 transport plan split over road versus rail funding and a permanent VAT surcharge.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/news/schweiz/verkehr-45-parteien-und-verbaende-wollen-nachbesserungen-beim-verkehrsausbau", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland", "politics"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "National parties, cantons and associations have filed their consultation responses to Verkehr '45, the Federal Council's first plan to prioritise rail, road and urban transport projects together up to 2045, SRF reported on Friday 9 October. None oppose it outright. The Greens and the SP welcome its tilt towards rail. The SVP calls that tilt an \"ideologically motivated imbalance\" at the expense of roads, and the FDP wants more balance. All parties except the SVP back the Federal Council's plan to make the temporary VAT surcharge for the rail infrastructure fund permanent; it currently expires in 2030. The first stage, in 2027, includes the first phase of Lucerne's through station, a fourth track at Zurich Stadelhofen and six lanes on the A1 between Perly and Bernex (GE). Zurich wants Stadelhofen built straight away, outside the package.", "why": "the open fight over the VAT surcharge and the road–rail split shows where Parliament's debate on the plan will be fought.", "thread_id": "2026-10-09-news-verkehr-45-draws-road-versus-rail-fight", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-09", "event_date": null, "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Verkehr '45", "Federal Council", "SVP"]}
